wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14616351898593479)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14493163251601159)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>23
,p_display_sequence=>90
,p_static_id=>'attribute_23'
,p_prompt=>'Patient & Observations Item'
,p_apexlang_name=>'contextSourceItem'
,p_attribute_type=>'PAGE ITEM'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14502628304154823)
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2('<p>Select a hidden, textarea or other text item containing plain JSON, populated by SQL, PL/SQL, a Dynamic Action or application code. Changes to the item refresh the summary. This is a display source in APEX; saved patient snapshots and examination prefills require an authorized Static JSON, SQL or PL/SQL source.</p><p><strong>Return one patient JSON object.</strong> Include identity and observations together; omit unused fields. Complete example (fictional):</p><pre>{"patient":{"name":"Demo patient (fictional)","mrn":"DEMO-CA3D-001","id":"DEMO-001","age":42,"sex":"Male","dateOfBirth":"1984-03-10","encounterId":"VISIT-DEMO-001","details":[{"id":"department","label":"Department","value":"General medicine"},{"id":"room","label":"Room","value":"A12"}]},"recording":{"source":"Nursing intake (demo)","recordedBy":"Demo nurse","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00"},"observations":[{"id":"bp_systolic","label":"Systolic BP","value":126,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_systolic"},{"id":"bp_diastolic","label":"Diastolic BP","value":78,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_diastolic"},{"id":"pulse","label":"Pulse","value":82,"unit":"beats/min","examField":"pulse"},{"id":"temperature","label":"Tempera',
'ture","value":36.8,"unit":"°C","examField":"temperature","readOnly":true},{"id":"weight","label":"Weight","value":72,"unit":"kg","examField":"weight","flag":"Review","highlight":true,"note":"Example review flag supplied by the source."},{"id":"height","label":"Height","value":175,"unit":"cm","examField":"height"},{"id":"spo2","label":"Oxygen saturation","value":98,"unit":"%","examField":"spo2"},{"id":"respiratory_rate","label":"Respiratory rate","value":16,"unit":"breaths/min","examField":"respiratory_rate"},{"id":"bmi","label":"BMI","value":23.5,"unit":"kg/m²"},{"id":"glucose","label":"Blood glucose","value":5.2,"unit":"mmol/L"},{"id":"pain","label":"Pain score","value":2,"unit":"/10"},{"id":"custom_observation","label":"Your custom label","value":"Your supplied value","unit":"","source":"Your source","recordedBy":"Your recorder","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00","flag":"","highlight":false,"readOnly":false,"hidden":true,"note":"Optional note","examField":"your_configured_exam_field"}]}</pre><p>patient: name, mrn, id, age (number in years), sex, dateOfBirth, encounterId, details (custom id/label/value/unit). recording supplies source/recordedBy/recordedAt defaults. observat',
'ions require unique id and scalar value (text, number, boolean or null). Optional label, unit, flag, highlight, readOnly, hidden, note, examField and recording overrides. Preset IDs and units are in the example; custom IDs/labels are supported. Age is supplied, not calculated.</p><p>Up to 40 observations, 12 patient details and 32767 payload characters. Null/empty values do not prefill. Matching examination fields/units are prefilled only when empty; existing answers/notes/deferrals are preserved. Flags/highlights come from your source; no thresholds or conversions are inferred. Display &amp; Prefill Options controls visibility, locking and saved snapshots.</p>'),null)
,p_depending_on_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14618227588808095)
,p_depending_on_has_to_exist=>true
,p_depending_on_condition_type=>'EQUALS'
,p_depending_on_expression=>'ITEM'
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14616484173593479)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14493163251601159)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>24
,p_display_sequence=>110
,p_static_id=>'attribute_24'
,p_prompt=>'Display & Prefill Options (JSON)'
,p_apexlang_name=>'contextOptions'
,p_attribute_type=>'TEXTAREA'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(14502628304154823)
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2('<p><strong>These are display and saving settings, not patient values.</strong> Patient values belong in Patient Data Source. Leave <code>{}</code> to use defaults. You do not need to configure this field to show supplied data.</p>
<ul><li><code>fields</code>: visible sections/identity keys. Default: all supplied fields. Choices: name, mrn, id, age, sex, dateOfBirth, encounterId, details, observations. details appear in the Details dialog.</li>
<li><code>labels</code>: replace identity labels, for example <code>{"mrn":"MRN","encounterId":"Encounter"}</code>.</li>
<li><code>observationIds</code>: show only these observation IDs in the summary and Details. Omit to show all supplied observations.</li>
<li><code>maxVisibleObservations</code>: 1–12 measurement cards above the viewer; default 6. Matching systolic/diastolic values share one BP card. The Details dialog shows the remaining visible observations without making the page taller.</li>
<li><code>prefillExam</code>: default true. Fill empty matching examination fields from observations. False displays values without filling examination answers. Existing values, notes and deferrals are preserved.</li>
<li><code>lockPrefilled</code>:',
' default false. True makes all imported examination values read only. A row''s readOnly can lock individual values. Notes remain editable.</li>
<li><code>patientDataRequired</code>: false by default. True blocks editing/saving if the patient source is unavailable; saved snapshots and prefill history always require server verification.</li><li><code>saveContext</code>: default false. True saves the complete patient/observation snapshot inside the anatomy JSON. Display filters do not remove hidden data from that snapshot. A saved snapshot takes precedence when reopening a record. False omits a new snapshot; prefilled examination answers are still saved, and an existing recorded snapshot is preserved.</li></ul>
<p>Use real JSON booleans (<code>true</code>/<code>false</code>), not quoted strings. Unknown options show a configuration message so mistakes can be corrected.</p><h3>Example</h3><pre>{
  "fields": [
    "name",
    "mrn",
    "age",
    "sex",
    "details",
    "observations"
  ],
  "labels": {
    "mrn": "MRN"
  },
  "observationIds": [
    "bp_systolic",
    "bp_diastolic",
    "pulse",
    "temperature",
    "weight",
    "height",
    "spo2",
    "respiratory_rate"
  ],
 ',
' "maxVisibleObservations": 6,
  "prefillExam": true,
  "lockPrefilled": false,
  "saveContext": true
}</pre>
<p>To show only patient identity, set <code>{"fields":["name","mrn","age"],"prefillExam":false}</code>. To keep defaults and save a snapshot, set <code>{"saveContext":true}</code>.</p>'),null)
,p_default_value=>'{}'
);
